IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part IV, "Administration and Enforcement" (s 44.2): what the Minister may examine and enter, the warrant needed to enter a dwelling-house,
-- the notice requiring a person to provide information or a document, the judge's authorization for a requirement about unnamed persons, the third party's
-- review, copies as evidence, and the prohibition on interfering.
-- Hohfeld: the Minister's power to examine, enter, and require information (44.2(2), (6)) is the owner's, occupant's or third party's liability; their duty to assist and
-- answer (44.2(2)(b)) and to comply with a notice is the Minister's claim; the occupant's immunity from entry without consent or warrant (44.2(3)) is the Minister's disability;
-- the third party's power to apply for review (44.2(10)) is the judge's and the Minister's liability; the prohibition in 44.2(13) is a duty on everyone.
-- The text states no penalty for interfering (44.2(13)), so that rule's penalty is NOTHING. Subsection 44.2(11) refers to "paragraphs (8)(a) to (d)", but
-- subsection 44.2(8) has only paragraphs (a) and (b); the encoding applies (a) and (b) (fork OA1-F16 of NOTES.md).

§ `Interpretation`

-- s 44.2(1) "document": the listed things and "other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics", and any copy or printout of any of them.
-- src:1096 | document includes moneys, securities, books, records, letters, accounts, statements (financial or otherwise), correspondence, memoranda, film, microform, videotape, photographs, machine-readable records and other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics, and any copy or printout of any of them. (document)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(1) "document" (src:1096)
GIVEN `the thing is moneys, securities, books, records, letters, accounts, statements (financial or otherwise), correspondence, memoranda, film, microform, videotape, photographs, machine-readable records or other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a copy or printout of any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(1): the thing is a document` `the thing is moneys, securities, books, records, letters, accounts, statements (financial or otherwise), correspondence, memoranda, film, microform, videotape, photographs, machine-readable records or other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics` `the thing is a copy or printout of any of them` MEANS
        `the thing is moneys, securities, books, records, letters, accounts, statements (financial or otherwise), correspondence, memoranda, film, microform, videotape, photographs, machine-readable records or other documentary material, regardless of form or characteristics`
    OR  `the thing is a copy or printout of any of them`

-- "dwelling-house": the whole or a part of a building or structure kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence, and (a) a building within its yard connected by a doorway or
-- covered and enclosed passageway, and (b) a mobile unit designed and used as a residence.
-- src:1097 | dwelling-house means the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence and includes
-- src:1098 | (a) a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway; and
-- src:1099 | (b) a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence. (maison d’habitation)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(1) "dwelling-house" (src:1097-1099)
GIVEN `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(1): the place is a dwelling-house` `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence` `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway` `the place is a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence` MEANS
        `the place is the whole or a part of a building or structure that is kept or occupied as a permanent or temporary residence`
    OR  `the place is a building within the yard of a dwelling-house that is connected to it by a doorway or by a covered and enclosed passageway`
    OR  `the place is a unit that is designed to be mobile and to be used as a permanent or temporary residence and that is being used as such a residence`

-- "judge": of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises, or of the Federal Court.
-- src:1100 | judge means a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises or a judge of the Federal Court. (juge)
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(1) "judge" (src:1100)
GIVEN `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(1): the person is a judge` `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises` `the person is a judge of the Federal Court` MEANS
        `the person is a judge of a superior court having jurisdiction in the province where the matter arises`
    OR  `the person is a judge of the Federal Court`

§ `Inspections`

-- s 44.2(2): at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, the Minister may examine any document that relates or may relate to
-- entitlement to a benefit or its amount.
-- src:1102 | (2) The Minister may, at any reasonable time, for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, examine any document that relates or may relate to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit and, for that purpose, the Minister may
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(2) (src:1102)
GIVEN `the time is a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document relates or may relate to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(2): the Minister may examine the document` `the time is a reasonable time` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the document relates or may relate to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit` MEANS
        `the time is a reasonable time`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the document relates or may relate to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of a benefit`

-- (3): a dwelling-house may not be entered without the occupant's consent, except under a warrant issued under subsection (4).
-- src:1106 | (3) If the premises or place referred to in subsection (2) is a dwelling-house, the Minister may not enter that dwelling-house without the consent of the occupant except under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection (4).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(3) (src:1106)
GIVEN `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the occupant consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 44.2(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(3): the Minister may enter the premises or place` `the premises or place is a dwelling-house` `the occupant consents` `the Minister acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 44.2(4)` MEANS
        (NOT `the premises or place is a dwelling-house`)
    OR  `the occupant consents`
    OR  `the Minister acts under the authority of a warrant issued under subsection 44.2(4)`

-- (2)(a): the Minister may enter any premises or place where the Minister believes a document relating to entitlement is or should be kept, subject to subsection (3).
-- src:1103 | (a) subject to subsection (3), enter any premises or place where the Minister believes a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of that benefit is or should be kept; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(2)(a) (src:1103)
GIVEN `the Minister believes a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of that benefit is or should be kept at the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 44.2(3) permits the Minister to enter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(2)(a): the Minister may enter the premises or place` `the Minister believes a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of that benefit is or should be kept at the premises or place` `subsection 44.2(3) permits the Minister to enter` MEANS
        `the Minister believes a document relating to the entitlement of a person to a benefit or the amount of that benefit is or should be kept at the premises or place`
    AND `subsection 44.2(3) permits the Minister to enter`

-- (2)(b): the Minister may require the owner, occupant or person in charge to give all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions relating to the administration or
-- enforcement of this Act, and attend at the premises or place with the Minister.
-- src:1104 | (b) require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to give the Minister all reasonable assistance and to answer all proper questions relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act and, for that purpose, require the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place to attend at those premises or that place with the Minister.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(2)(b) (src:1104)
GIVEN `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is examining a document or entering under subsection 44.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(2)(b): the Minister may require the person to give all reasonable assistance, answer all proper questions and attend at the premises or place with the Minister` `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place` `the Minister is examining a document or entering under subsection 44.2(2)` `the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of this Act` MEANS
        `the person is the owner, occupant or person in charge of the premises or place`
    AND `the Minister is examining a document or entering under subsection 44.2(2)`
    AND `the questions relate to the administration or enforcement of this Act`

§ `Warrants`

-- (4): on the Minister's ex parte application, a judge may issue a warrant if satisfied by information on oath of (a), (b) and (c).
-- src:1108 | (4) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter a dwelling-house subject to the conditions that may be specified in the warrant, if the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1109 | (a) there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection (2);
-- src:1110 | (b) entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act; and
-- src:1111 | (c) entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(4) (src:1108-1111)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 44.2(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(4): a judge may issue a warrant authorizing the Minister to enter the dwelling-house` `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 44.2(2)` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused` MEANS
        `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the dwelling-house is a premises or place referred to in subsection 44.2(2)`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that entry into the dwelling-house has been refused or that there are reasonable grounds to believe that entry will be refused`

-- (5): the judge is not satisfied that entry is necessary but is satisfied that access to a document has been or may be expected to be refused.
-- src:1113 | (5) If the judge is not satisfied that entry into that dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act but is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused, the judge may
-- src:1114 | (a) order the occupant of the dwelling-house to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document; and
-- src:1115 | (b) make any other order that is appropriate in the circumstances to carry out the purposes of this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(5) (src:1113-1115)
GIVEN `the judge is satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(5): the judge may order the occupant to provide the Minister with reasonable access to the document and make any other appropriate order` `the judge is satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused` MEANS
        (NOT `the judge is satisfied that entry into the dwelling-house is necessary for a purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act`)
    AND `the judge is satisfied that access to a document that is or should be kept in the dwelling-house has been or may be expected to be refused`

§ `Requirement to provide documents or information`

-- (7): a requirement relating to unnamed persons needs the judge's authorization first.
-- src:1119 | (7) The Minister shall not impose on a person, in this section referred to as a “third party”, a requirement under subsection (6) to provide information or a document relating to one or more unnamed persons unless the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection (8).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(7) (src:1119)
GIVEN `the requirement is to provide information or a document relating to one or more unnamed persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection 44.2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(7): the Minister may impose the requirement on the third party` `the requirement is to provide information or a document relating to one or more unnamed persons` `the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection 44.2(8)` MEANS
        (NOT `the requirement is to provide information or a document relating to one or more unnamed persons`)
    OR  `the Minister first obtains the authorization of a judge under subsection 44.2(8)`

-- (6): by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, within a reasonable time stipulated in the notice, for any purpose relating to administration or enforcement,
-- subject to subsection (7).
-- src:1117 | (6) Despite any other provision of this Act, the Minister may, subject to subsection (7), for any purpose relating to the administration or enforcement of this Act, by notice served personally or by confirmed delivery service, require that any person provide, within the reasonable time that is stipulated in the notice, any information or additional information or any document.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(6) (src:1117)
GIVEN `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice stipulates a reasonable time within which the person is to provide the information or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 44.2(7) permits the Minister to impose the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(6): the Minister may require the person to provide the information, additional information or document` `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service` `the notice stipulates a reasonable time within which the person is to provide the information or document` `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act` `subsection 44.2(7) permits the Minister to impose the requirement` MEANS
        `the notice is served personally or by confirmed delivery service`
    AND `the notice stipulates a reasonable time within which the person is to provide the information or document`
    AND `the purpose relates to the administration or enforcement of this Act`
    AND `subsection 44.2(7) permits the Minister to impose the requirement`

-- (8): on the Minister's ex parte application, a judge may authorize a requirement relating to unnamed persons if satisfied by information on oath that (a) the person or group is
-- ascertainable and (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance with a duty or obligation under this Act.
-- src:1121 | (8) On ex parte application by the Minister, a judge may, subject to the conditions that the judge considers appropriate, authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement under subsection (6) relating to one or more unnamed persons, in this section referred to as the “group”, where the judge is satisfied by information on oath that
-- src:1122 | (a) the person or group is ascertainable; and
-- src:1123 | (b) the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(8) (src:1121-1123)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(8): a judge may authorize the Minister to impose on a third party a requirement relating to one or more unnamed persons` `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable` `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act` MEANS
        `the application is made ex parte by the Minister to a judge`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the person or group is ascertainable`
    AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath that the requirement is made to verify compliance by the person or persons in the group with a duty or obligation under this Act`

-- (9): a granted authorization is served together with the notice.
-- src:1125 | (9) If an authorization is granted under subsection (8), the authorization shall be served together with the notice referred to in subsection (6).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(9) (src:1125)
GIVEN `an authorization is granted under subsection 44.2(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorization is served together with the notice referred to in subsection 44.2(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(9): the authorization has been served as the Act requires` `an authorization is granted under subsection 44.2(8)` `the authorization is served together with the notice referred to in subsection 44.2(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `an authorization is granted under subsection 44.2(8)`)
    OR  `the authorization is served together with the notice referred to in subsection 44.2(6)`

-- (10): the third party may apply for review "not later than 15 days after the service of the notice".
-- "not later than 15 days after": the day that is fifteen days after is the last day (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:1127 | (10) If an authorization is granted under subsection (8), a third party on whom a notice is served under subsection (6) may, not later than 15 days after the service of the notice, apply to the judge who granted the authorization or, if that judge is unable to act, to another judge of the same court, for a review of the authorization.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(10) (src:1127)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice is served` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the third party applies for a review of the authorization` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(10): the third party may apply for a review of the authorization on the day` `the day on which the notice is served` `the day on which the third party applies for a review of the authorization` MEANS
        `the day on which the third party applies for a review of the authorization` AT LEAST `the day on which the notice is served`
    AND `the day on which the third party applies for a review of the authorization` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 15) `after` `the day on which the notice is served`)

-- (11): on hearing the application the judge may cancel the authorization if no longer satisfied of the conditions in (8), and may confirm or vary it if satisfied.
-- src:1129 | (11) On hearing an application under subsection (10), a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (8)(a) to (d) have been met, and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if the judge is satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(11) (src:1129)
GIVEN `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(11): the judge may cancel the authorization previously granted` `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met` MEANS
    `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met`

-- src:1129 | (11) On hearing an application under subsection (10), a judge may cancel the authorization previously granted if the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs (8)(a) to (d) have been met, and the judge may confirm or vary the authorization if the judge is satisfied that those conditions have been met.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(11) (src:1129)
GIVEN `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(11): the judge may confirm or vary the authorization` `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met` MEANS
    NOT `the judge is not then satisfied that the conditions in paragraphs 44.2(8)(a) to (d) have been met`

§ `Evidence and compliance`

-- (12): a certified copy made by the person who inspected, examined or was provided the document is evidence of its nature and content and has the same probative force.
-- src:1131 | (12) When a document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with this section, the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided may make, or cause to be made, one or more certified copies of it and any such copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(12) (src:1131)
GIVEN `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 44.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is made, or caused to be made, by the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(12): the copy is evidence of the nature and content of the original document and has the same probative force as the original` `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 44.2` `the copy is made, or caused to be made, by the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided` `the copy is certified` MEANS
        `the document is inspected, examined or provided in accordance with section 44.2`
    AND `the copy is made, or caused to be made, by the person by whom it is inspected or examined or to whom it is provided`
    AND `the copy is certified`

-- (13): no person shall interfere with a person doing anything the person is authorized under section 44.2 to do, or prevent or attempt to prevent it.
-- src:1133 | (13) No person shall interfere with any person doing anything that the person is authorized under this section to do or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(13) (src:1133)
GIVEN `the other person is doing something that they are authorized under section 44.2 to do` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person interferes with the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person prevents or attempts to prevent the other person from doing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 44.2(13): the person has contravened the prohibition` `the other person is doing something that they are authorized under section 44.2 to do` `the person interferes with the other person` `the person prevents or attempts to prevent the other person from doing it` MEANS
        `the other person is doing something that they are authorized under section 44.2 to do`
    AND (    `the person interferes with the other person`
         OR  `the person prevents or attempts to prevent the other person from doing it`)

-- The text states no penalty for the contravention (it is not one of the acts in section 44(1)): NOTHING.
-- src:1133 | (13) No person shall interfere with any person doing anything that the person is authorized under this section to do or prevent or attempt to prevent any person from doing any such thing.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 44.2(13) (src:1133)
GIVEN `the person has contravened subsection 44.2(13)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 44.2(13): the greatest fine that this Act sets for the contravention` `the person has contravened subsection 44.2(13)` MEANS
    NOTHING
